#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110374 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dee17b1d-686f-5817-b7dd-bf5b0bbd3da3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Segments on a Number Line"}] :question/id #uuid "8d23b33d-46ad-56af-853c-353c306c7af0" :question/math-academy-id "e-2553" :question/problem "![](images/8b/8bc5a70179a245c26f766e7c0efb36b508d259746a6a92b02c4d423d39940d5a.png)\n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $AC=BD$\n2. $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$\n3. $\\overline{AB}$ is congruent to $\\overline{BD}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that $AC= BD=5$ units.\n- Statement II is true. Since $AB=CD=3$ units, we have that $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$.\n- Statement III is false since $AB=3$, while $BD = 5$. So, $\\overline{AB}\\ncong \\overline{BD}$.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110375 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb023488-e5ec-5d04-9cc2-b40db799887c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Line Segments on a Grid"}] :question/id #uuid "a53bc0ac-2deb-53f9-a4cf-2ac02b903cd2" :question/math-academy-id "e-2554" :question/problem "Which of the line segments shown below are congruent?\n\n![](images/fe/fea89643ee848c5cce4ea9844da71fae26f4799c4dbbe5795086a5365fbf3ec9.png)" :question/worked-solution "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB = 3$ units\n- $CD=EF = 4$ units\n- $GH = 2$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent line segments is $\\overline{CD}\\cong\\overline{EF}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69275189-af69-51ce-bfc0-5f03976c117f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Line Segments on a Given Plane Figure"}] :question/id #uuid "e5cdb5e0-0ea7-5a96-81d4-0b53e2ad2f9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-2556" :question/problem "For the diagram shown below, which of the following statements are true?\n\n![](images/79/793dacde520b1be4aa4a1e023760a06d1db5fe23266ec1277efe948e8ca04ab1.png)\n\n1. The segments $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ are congruent\n2. $\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BE}$\n3. $BE = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. In the picture, both $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have the same double hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BD}$.\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, we can see that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BC}$ have different hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BC} \\not\\cong \\overline{BE}$.\n- Statement III is false. According to the picture, we have that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have different hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BE} \\not\\cong \\overline{BD}$.\nHence, ${BE} \\neq {BD}$, and since ${BD} = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$, we have $BE \\neq 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}]}
